  "status_text": "The step the hunt has been chasing is no longer a wall at the size we can list (computed, not checked). On every cheapest circuit found for the 5-cycle, fixing one input makes three gates go, and each time the third is simply a wire nobody reads any more once its only reader is dead. What remains is one checked lemma, one on the desk, and one fact about cheapest circuits still to prove. On the crown, what all 681 cheapest circuits do at four a side went to the desk as a statement for every size, for anyone to prove or break: each input is read exactly once.",
